description:
Implement a `usePortal` hook that returns a `Portal` component. `Portal` renders its children into a given `container` element (defaults to `document.body`) using `ReactDOM.createPortal`.

**Example:**
```tsx
const { Portal } = usePortal();
return (
  <div>
    <Portal>
      <Modal />
    </Portal>
  </div>
);
// Modal is rendered into document.body, not inside the div
```

